  "body": "## Research: local-move exhaustion on the pivot-566+554 T74 supplier, and idle-optimality of the 249/417 dispatch (no new \u03ba)\n\nSince PR1800, \u03ba \u2248 b(supplier) up to the free slacks, so only a cheaper T74 supplier can raise it. This package gives exact, reproducible negative results for the cheap local move families on the current base and extra words, which are the same bytes as PR1839/PR1672. It also gives an ILP certificate that the owner packing's idle side is already optimal.\n\n**Results** (`research/t74-k554-local-exhaustion/RESULTS.json`; raw data in `data/`)\n\n- **Deletion relaxation of all 1,797 B reads** (exact frames). 1,002 deletions would lower cost.\n  - Exactly 16 save one rank-2 split (\u22124,913 units): the early pivot reads of 448/450/452/454/585/587/589/591/473/497/521/545/586/588, plus the two costly reads inside the 566/554 kernels (B1, B3).\n  - The rest are delivery reads, first writes and structural reads, from \u22123,050 to \u221226,389.\n  - All 1,002 send value into target rows, so compensation must stay inside B. None can be moved to the frame-free cleanup prepends.\n- **Frame-cost oracle**, calibrated exactly on PR1672's pivot-554 kernel. Its insert costs are `[0, 4913, 0, 0]`, so the kernel's whole cost is one rank-2 split. The cost-aware search rediscovers a \u22121,850 kernel by itself.\n- **107 cost-aware compensation searches:** no negative delta. Every one-split read needs at least one split to compensate. Large-gain reads have single-window source values or rows that no candidate can reach.\n- **Exact single-gate commuting-move sweep:** all 1,002 gain-carrying reads at all 4,461 window positions, exact solver. Results: 2,131 neutral, 2,330 infeasible, **0 gains**.\n- **A section:**\n  - A1220/1226/1232/1238/1244 are cold-pivot pre-cancels, each saving 6,763 if deleted. Compensating them across A, B and tails, with full-program exactness and the dirt rule, is infeasible.\n  - 91 rewrites of a cancelling read pair into reads of the pivot's writer are all frame-infeasible.\n- **Owner packing (aggregate ILP over all T74 child windows):**\n  - Moving any K = 12, 24, \u2026 extra calls to base is infeasible.\n  - Over every mix of the 0\u20134 entrance-demotion variants (W_res 3734\u20133738), the maximum number of empty rank-48 children is **22,748**. That is the current value, attained by 249 base / 417 extra.\n  - So no supplier-mix or modulo-48 rebalancing can add idle rank-48 children.\n\n**Reproduce:** `python3 -B research/t74-k554-local-exhaustion/verify.py --work /abs/new/work`. It takes about 5 minutes on 2 cores and checks:\n- pins and profiles;\n- the oracle calibration;\n- 32+32 sampled exact re-solves;\n- the 16 one-split searches;\n- the packing ILPs;\n- result consistency.\n\n`--full` re-solves everything and takes several CPU hours. The receipt is in `evidence/`.\n\n**Scope:** finite searches of the stated move families on two fixed words. This does not rule out multi-gate rewrites outside these families, new kernel mechanisms, or parent/centre-interface changes such as centre-path sharing (PR1708/1748/1791). No \u03ba is claimed and no construction is changed.\n\n**Credit:** PR1186 (toolkit, vendored verbatim), PR1625 (mdumitrean), PR1672 (jeremykothe2 / LeverRank), PR1319/PR1297/PR1193, and PR1839/PR1800. Prepared by Rohan Arun with substantial AI assistance (Anthropic Claude). Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TGoMCHAqctZe4wtb4qr7vv\n",
